---
import Icon from "@/components/icon.astro";
import Docs from "@/layouts/docs.astro";
import { examples } from "@/lib/examples";
---

<Docs title="Live examples" description="Examples that run the StateWalker VCS packages in your browser: commits, branches and merges, Git's object bytes, a real .git directory, and the Git protocol between two repositories." wide>
  <h1>Live examples</h1>
  <p>
    Each example below is a small TypeScript module that runs in this tab, on this repository's
    packages (the code published to npm, built from the main branch). Its page shows the module's source and a <strong>Run</strong> button: the code
    you read is the code that runs. Nothing is sent to a server; there is no server.
  </p>

  <div class="not-prose my-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {examples.map((example, i) => (
      <a href={`/examples/${example.name}`} class="group rounded-xl border bg-card p-5 text-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-primary/50">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-primary">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</p>
        <p class="mt-1 font-semibold">{example.label}</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">{example.summary}</p>
        <p class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-primary">
          Open and run <Icon name="arrowRight" class="size-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" />
        </p>
      </a>
    ))}
    <a href="/examples/playground" class="group rounded-xl border border-primary/40 bg-primary/5 p-5 text-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-primary">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs text-primary">PLAYGROUND</p>
      <p class="mt-1 font-semibold">Drive a repository yourself</p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Edit files, stage and commit, create and switch branches, merge them, and watch the log and
        status as you go, all in memory in this tab.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium text-primary">
        Open the playground <Icon name="arrowRight" class="size-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" />
      </p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <h2>How they run</h2>
  <p>
    The site is built with Astro and Vite, which bundle each example with the workspace packages
    it imports (<code>@statewalker/vcs-core</code>, <code>vcs-working-tree</code>,
    <code>vcs-commands</code>, <code>vcs-store-files</code>, <code>vcs-transport</code>). The
    packages use only APIs that browsers and servers share (a <code>FilesApi</code> for files,
    Web Streams, Web Crypto, <code>fetch</code>), so no shim is involved. A browser check
    (<code>site/scripts/check-examples.mjs</code>) runs every example on every change to the site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each example page ends with links to the concepts it shows; they are collected in
    <a href="/docs/concepts">How Git works here</a>. For longer programs, the repository has
    eleven numbered Node tutorials and eleven demos: see <a href="/docs/examples">Apps &amp; demos</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
